 where needed (","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int128","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for fixed-width","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integers, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"code":"Float","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), so a contracted group’s connection may pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s range.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every capacity is at least zero, not NaN and finite, and the minimum cut’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value fits in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"text":" (it is at most every vertex’s capacity sum).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A global minimum cut, over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directed"},{"type":"text","text":": the least capacity of the edges between a nonempty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"proper vertex set and the rest, the set holding the first vertex as the source side; nil"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"below two vertices. By Nagamochi–Ibaraki (LEMON "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NagamochiIbaraki"},{"type":"text","text":"; the same value as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stoer_wagner"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stoer_wagner_min_cut"},{"type":"text","text":", rustworkx "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stoer_wagner_min_cut"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and igraph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mincut()"},{"type":"text","text":"): maximum adjacency orderings that contract every edge whose scanned"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connection is at least the best cut so far, so later phases run on smaller graphs. Which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minimum cut is returned when several exist is not specified, but the same input always"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gives the same cut. When the edges of positive capacity do not connect the graph, the cut"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of value zero whose source side is the first vertex’s component, with every crossing edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(all of capacity zero). Parallel capacities add; self-loops are ignored. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called once per non-loop edge, in position order, before any work (self-loops are never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asked). O(nm log n) in the worst case, far less when contractions are many."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumcut(capacity:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows","doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumCut(capacity:)"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"GlobalMinimumCut.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Flows\/GlobalMinimumCut.swift#L483"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5FlowsE10minimumCut8capacityAD0E0VyAA12DirectedViewVyxGqd__GSgqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumCut"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text